{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1480609-combatting-spirits-with-normal-weapons","id":1480609,"title":"Combatting Spirits with normal weapons","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-09T18:03:52-07:00","id":1480609,"title":"Combatting Spirits with normal weapons","content":"Hi there,<br /> <br /> When you're in the Umbra and you undedicate a weapon such as a sword or a knife, or even a gun -- do they have any impact on spirits during combat? I was always of the mind frame that natural weaponry, gifts, or fetishes is the way to go and that weapons like a sword or a gun won't have any effect or hurt them. <br /> <br /> Can I get a ruling from the hive mind? <br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23998-dynamiterave","name":"DynamiteRave","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-09T19:44:44-07:00","id":1480620,"title":"","content":"I always house rule If you are in the same dimension as them you can damage them with normal weaponary unless the spirit has some form of intangibility, dispersated body or instant regeneration.<br /> <br /> Having access to agravated damage is the way to bypass this be it trought magical powers or the usage of the spirit bane who will be highly effective against them. Fire is a common bane in my games because it represents prometheus fire and the divine that is inside humankind so it pushes most false gods/spirits away bringing light to the darknes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-09T20:04:56-07:00","id":1480622,"title":"","content":"There's nothing in the rules that suggest that mundane weapons brought into the Umbra don't work on spirits or other supernatural entities in the Umbra. Natural weaponry, Gifts, and relevant Fetishes are preferred because they're more effective and spirit combat is pretty dangerous in most editions.<br /> <br /> A lot of spirits also have Charms that can easily destroy or control technology; which is another reason not to get overly reliant on human style weapons when fighting spirits.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-10T04:02:29-07:00","id":1480653,"title":"","content":"How would one bring an undedicated weapon into the umbra?<br /> This bag-fetisch W20 cooked up? Or the Tractor Beam gift?<br /> <br /> Anyway, I would argue, that they work just as normal. Like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> stated, there is nothing that suggests against spirits or other entities in the Umbra - and I might add, the umbrascape as well. I mean, if you brought mundane explosives into the umbra they would still level an penumbral house. It might be back in a later scene, but for the current scene it will be damaged (and this might slightly leak back into the physical world).<br /> <br /> Same goes into the other direction, too. You can pick up a stone made of epherma, bring it to the physical world and throw it at a formorer's head. Sure, the stone will dissolve eventually, but for a few rounds it usually is a stone that works just fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-10T12:46:33-07:00","id":1480685,"title":"","content":"The bag in W20 is just condensing a bunch of similar Fetishes that have been around since 2e. So, basically, Garou have always had relatively easy ways to bring some undedicated stuff into the Umbra. Though the OP did suggest undedicating something once you were already in the Umbra (why do that I have no idea).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-10T14:11:10-07:00","id":1480690,"title":"","content":"You can bring in undedicated people and items into the Umbra. The fourth level Gift Grasp From Beyond does that (and allows them to cross back again). Objects brought into the Umbra work just as they do normally. It's not explicit, but we're not told they don't and is pretty much the point of the Gift. It's just if they are left over time in the Umbra, the slowly transform from matter into ephemera. I'd have the same thing apply in the OP's scenario.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-11T01:25:50-07:00","id":1480733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1480609-combatting-spirits-with-normal-weapons?p=1480685#post1480685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The bag in W20 is just condensing a bunch of similar Fetishes that have been around since 2e</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you have any examples?<br /> I can remember &quot;Tractor Beam&quot; as a Gift and sure, &quot;Parting the Velvet Curtain&quot; Gift to bring over, for example, kinfolk, wouldn't leave them naked - I guess. &quot;Grasp of the Beyond&quot; consolidates this.<br /> <br /> But other fetishes I can't remember....<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-11T02:03:26-07:00","id":1480734,"title":"","content":"The Gnawers had a gym bag, the Glass Walkers a briefcase, and so on in the original Tribeboks IIRC. Those were eventually combined into the Magpie's Swag in Revised.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-11T13:39:24-07:00","id":1480761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1480609-combatting-spirits-with-normal-weapons?p=1480653#post1480653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would one bring an undedicated weapon into the umbra?<br /> This bag-fetisch W20 cooked up? Or the Tractor Beam gift?<br /> <br /> Anyway, I would argue, that they work just as normal. Like <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> stated, there is nothing that suggests against spirits or other entities in the Umbra - and I might add, the umbrascape as well. I mean, if you brought mundane explosives into the umbra they would still level an penumbral house. It might be back in a later scene, but for the current scene it will be damaged (and this might slightly leak back into the physical world).<br /> <br /> Same goes into the other direction, too. You can pick up a stone made of epherma, bring it to the physical world and throw it at a formorer's head. Sure, the stone will dissolve eventually, but for a few rounds it usually is a stone that works just fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant to say if they un-dedicate the weapon after they cross over. So for example they pop into the umbra and pull a sword out of dedication, is that sword or a gun going to be really effective against a bane. <br /> <br /> I take it that they most likely do lethal damage, right? Do banes/spirits tend to shrug that type of damage off since it's not aggravated? I'm still a bit new to story telling spirit combatants so I am hoping to make an upcoming scene fun. We have one guy who wants to use a sword for whatever reason <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23998-dynamiterave","name":"DynamiteRave","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-12T00:21:59-07:00","id":1480812,"title":"","content":"Generally, spirits don't make a difference regarding the type of damage. All damage is subtracted from Essence equally and Essence is restored all the same.<br /> <br /> It shouldn't make a difference, whether the fangs and teeth injure a spirit, or a blade or a tackle or a wall toppled on the spirit. In most cases, that is. For certain spirits it could make sense to give them certain resistances or immunities to highlight their themes.<br /> <br /> Attacking a fire elemental with &quot;Create Element: Fire&quot; not that effective probably. &quot;Create Element: Water&quot; usually not causing damage, but in this case, maybe it should.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 05-12-2022, 03:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-12T01:29:25-07:00","id":1480813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1480609-combatting-spirits-with-normal-weapons?p=1480812#post1480812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Generally, spirits don't make a difference regarding the type of damage. All damage is subtracted from Essence equally and Essence is restored all the same.<br /> <br /> It shouldn't make a difference, whether the fangs and teeth injure a spirit, or a blade or a tackle or a wall toppled on the spirit. In most cases, that is. For certain spirits it could make sense to give them certain resistances or immunities to highlight their themes.<br /> <br /> Attacking a fire elemental with &quot;Create Element: Fire&quot; not that effective probably. &quot;Create Element: Water&quot; usually not causing damage, but in this case, maybe it should.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, the spirits are vulnerable to damage like any other being, but their nature should give balance. A fire elemental shoud not be able to soak damage from water type attack and they should be injured by being in wet environnement. <br /> However, regarding their damage to characters, are they aggravated? Does a wolf spirit's claw inflict aggravated damage or do they need a specific charm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-12T01:48:59-07:00","id":1480814,"title":"","content":"W20 doesn't specify the damage type on page 365/366. I'd argue it should be determined by storytelling need. A kitten spirit should probably not inflict aggravated damage, a wolf spirit should. Fang and Claw, in tendency, should be aggravated, while slam attacks more likely should inflict normal damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-12T02:38:12-07:00","id":1480818,"title":"","content":"Also remember that spirits are not Pokemon. While the rules provide us with broad templates, they're supposed to be unique entities. Just because a spirit has a fire association doesn't mean it's weak to water attacks. That's CCG/video game logic, not animist spirit world logic. WtA doesn't really worry about such things because the Garou are already built to be able to fight spirits without trying to attack them with Super Effective &quot;types&quot; of damage. Garou that specialize in spirit combat push things even farther into not needing that sort of mechanic.<br /> <br /> If you really want that sort of thing, you can just port the Bane system for spirits from the CofD: which has guidance for how specific/broad such things should be to match the power and broadness of the spirit. Just make Banes do unsoakable damage and be ready for Theurge players to bombard you with rolls to know what to use.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-12T12:50:10-07:00","id":1480853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1480609-combatting-spirits-with-normal-weapons?p=1480818#post1480818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also remember that spirits are not Pokemon. While the rules provide us with broad templates, they're supposed to be unique entities. Just because a spirit has a fire association doesn't mean it's weak to water attacks. That's CCG/video game logic, not animist spirit world logic. WtA doesn't really worry about such things because the Garou are already built to be able to fight spirits without trying to attack them with Super Effective &quot;types&quot; of damage. Garou that specialize in spirit combat push things even farther into not needing that sort of mechanic.<br /> <br /> If you really want that sort of thing, you can just port the <b>Bane system</b> for spirits from the CofD: which has guidance for how specific/broad such things should be to match the power and broadness of the spirit. Just make Banes do unsoakable damage and be ready for Theurge players to bombard you with rolls to know what to use.</div> </div> </div> </div>That name is bound to cause some confusion at least part of the time in W:tA...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-12T13:15:03-07:00","id":1480857,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=DynamiteRave;n1480761]<br /> I meant to say if they <u><b>un-dedicate</b></u> the weapon after they cross over. So for example they pop into the umbra and pull a sword out of dedication, is that sword or a gun going to be really effective against a bane.<br /> /QUOTE]<br /> <br /> &quot;This word you keep using; I do not think it means what you think it means.&quot; - <i>Inigo Montoya to Vizini in The Princess Bride</i>.<br /> <br /> I couldn't resist using that quote. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Garou dedicate items so that they will shift forms with them and accompany them into the umbra, but un-dedicating is not required to use them. The Garou in question simply shifts to a form that can use the item and it will appear ready to be used.<br /> <br /> Un-dedicating an item means that it will no longer stay with you when you shift forms and will fall to the ground on the side you are leaving when you cross the gauntlet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/693-thomasm","name":"ThomasM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar693_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-12T13:19:12-07:00","id":1480858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1480609-combatting-spirits-with-normal-weapons?p=1480853#post1480853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That name is bound to cause some confusion at least part of the time in W:tA...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's why I said &quot;system&quot; not, &quot;totality.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ThomasM</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1480609-combatting-spirits-with-normal-weapons?p=1480857#post1480857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Garou dedicate items so that they will shift forms with them and accompany them into the umbra, but un-dedicating is not required to use them.</div> </div> </div> </div>While this is true 99% of the time, the game does allow &quot;sets&quot; of items to be dedicated and the ST can rule that removing something from the set can undedicate it. So if you have a dedicated wallet with $40 in cash in it, and you give the cash to a spirit as chiminage, the cash stops being part of the wallet-set and thus is no longer dedicated. Most STs aren't such nitpickers to claim this applies to a blade and a sheath though.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-12T13:32:22-07:00","id":1480859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1480609-combatting-spirits-with-normal-weapons?p=1480858#post1480858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While this is true 99% of the time, the game does allow &quot;sets&quot; of items to be dedicated and the ST can rule that removing something from the set can undedicate it. So if you have a dedicated wallet with $40 in cash in it, and you give the cash to a spirit as chiminage, the cash stops being part of the wallet-set and thus is no longer dedicated. Most STs aren't such nitpickers to claim this applies to a blade and a sheath though.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;You are technically correct; the best kind of correct.&quot; - Inspector 1.0 to Hermes Conrad in the Futurama episode &quot;How Hermes Requisitioned His Groove Back&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/693-thomasm","name":"ThomasM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar693_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-12T17:24:57-07:00","id":1480899,"title":"","content":"Well, if they are in the same realm, I, as ST would rule it accordingly to the spirit's nature, e.g. if t's a fire salamander, I wouldn't allow it to be hurt by a sword attack or gunshots, as imo it would make no fucking sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-12T23:07:42-07:00","id":1480937,"title":"","content":"It doesn't make sense according to what?<br /> <br /> WtA spirits don't have &quot;health&quot; or wound penalties. You're not chopping up their internal organs (they don't actually have those either). Damaging them is forcing them to exert their nature (lose Essence) to maintain their form. If you damage them enough, they need to go somewhere to recharge (and unless you have a power to stop that, they'll do so fairly easily).<br /> <br /> If I do six damage to a human, they're Crippled and suffering from massive penalties to any actions, on top of being close to incapacitation. If I do six damage to a spirit, it loses six Essence, and can then hit me back at full strength or whatever it's up to. Maybe, if it's low enough on Essence, it can't whip out it's most powerful Charms (or use a Charm to maximum effect). <br /> <br /> We're also still talking about WtA here... how many WtA PCs are getting into fights with spirits, using Firearms or Melee based weapons, and not using magical weapons as it is?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-12T23:23:06-07:00","id":1480938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1480609-combatting-spirits-with-normal-weapons?p=1480937#post1480937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't make sense according to what?<br /> <br /> WtA spirits don't have &quot;health&quot; or wound penalties. You're not chopping up their internal organs (they don't actually have those either). Damaging them is forcing them to exert their nature (lose Essence) to maintain their form. If you damage them enough, they need to go somewhere to recharge (and unless you have a power to stop that, they'll do so fairly easily).<br /> <br /> If I do six damage to a human, they're Crippled and suffering from massive penalties to any actions, on top of being close to incapacitation. If I do six damage to a spirit, it loses six Essence, and can then hit me back at full strength or whatever it's up to. Maybe, if it's low enough on Essence, it can't whip out it's most powerful Charms (or use a Charm to maximum effect).<br /> <br /> We're also still talking about WtA here... how many WtA PCs are getting into fights with spirits, using Firearms or Melee based weapons, and not using magical weapons as it is?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sense according to logic, how are you supposed to damage fire with a sword?? Even more so, a mundane sword!? lol...<br /> The only explanation as to why werewolves are capable of hurting spirits with their claws is that werewolves are half-spirit/half-physical.<br /> What you imply would make someone wonder if they can go about &quot;kicking wraiths just because...&quot;, or you can hit someone who turned to mist with a kick and cause damage, even though the books state otherwise...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","user":"Herr Meister","date":". 05-13-2022, 02:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-13T00:15:29-07:00","id":1480943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1480609-combatting-spirits-with-normal-weapons?p=1480937#post1480937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WtA spirits don't have &quot;health&quot; or wound penalties. You're not chopping up their internal organs (they don't actually have those either). Damaging them is forcing them to exert their nature (lose Essence) to maintain their form. If you damage them enough, they need to go somewhere to recharge (and unless you have a power to stop that, they'll do so fairly easily).</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but I guess this removes something from the game that I think, wasn't intentional. The very abstract combat system isn't focused on the narrative qualities of combat actions a in a way that cool descriptions of what you aim to do get you bonuses on attack rolls or damage rolls if you increase the difficulty or something like that. WtA has combat maneuvers, but not to the extend WoD: Combat offers.<br /> <br /> So, going for the eys, the joints, the head to smash the brains in, or similar approaches should be working for most spirits, too - from a narrative standpoint. That is, if the spirit has such things. If the spirit is just a string of silvery light swirling around, then well .... just hit it with something.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> The whole Rite of Dedication thing is open to some strange interpretations. I would argue, that the sword is the significant object to be dedicated, the sheath is a related object that makes sense to be in a set with the blade. But drawing the sword, even handing it over to a kinfolk so it can be cleaned and re-sharpened doesn't end the dedication. Abandoning it (in a metal or spiritual sense) would, I guess, as would &quot;coming to the realisation that it was taken/stolen from you&quot;. Garou mysticism is supposed to be intuitive in contrast to hermetic magic with it's strict rules.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-13T01:48:37-07:00","id":1480948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1480609-combatting-spirits-with-normal-weapons?p=1480938#post1480938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sense according to logic, how are you supposed to damage fire with a sword?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not using logic, you're trying to dress up your opinions and preferences as logic. The sword isn't fighting fire, it's fighting a fire-spirit. Those aren't the same things. How does a Garou bite a fire-spirit and hurt it? Can you hurt fire with your teeth? The spirits we're talking about are part of a massive animist cosmology. That's the defining logic of how things work; not what a human with a mundane sword can do swinging it at a flame; because that's not what's happening.<br /> <br /> When Garou bring themselves and their belongings into the Umbra (or a spirit manifests in the material plane) everything is on the same &quot;wavelength.&quot; The sword can cut the <b>spirit</b> of fire because spirits aren't just animated raw materials. They are entities from another plane of existence with their own substance and magical-physiology.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The only explanation as to why werewolves are capable of hurting spirits with their claws is that werewolves are half-spirit/half-physical. </div> </div> </div>Even without getting into anything Mage related, there are lots of ways beings that aren't &quot;half&quot; of both worlds can harm beings of the other world if they're brought into the same plane. Garou are really good at hurting spirits because of their own spiritual nature, but if a spirit manifests in the physical world a kin can still shot it, and damage it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What you imply would make someone wonder if they can go about &quot;kicking wraiths just because...&quot;, </div> </div> </div>I have no idea what that even means. But if one of the Quick ends up in the Shadowlands, they can absolutely get in combat with a Wraith and harm it. But Wraiths have corpus. They have a reflection of their mortal selves that they're attached to enough that hurting it hurts them. You don't just drain them of Pathos until they disembody and go rest up for a bit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> or you can hit someone who turned to mist with a kick and cause damage, even though the books state otherwise... </div> </div> </div>This is a crap argument. If a power says the user is immune to physical harm (or immune with exceptions) than that's what it is. Kicking a vampire using Protean 5 doesn't do you any good.<br /> <br /> Spirits <b>are not stated to have this benefit</b> therefore they don't. Maybe instead of insisting they have powers they don't have, you should try to reconcile what the games are actually saying spirits are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1480609-combatting-spirits-with-normal-weapons?p=1480943#post1480943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, but I guess this removes something from the game that I think, wasn't intentional.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's being removed from the game by mundane weapons brought into the Umbra working in spirit-combat when that's always been the rules? Even if it wasn't intentional in 1e, they never changed it. Even the CofD didn't fully change this despite changing other things around this that shows that the developers were aware of it.<br /> <br /> I fail to see a compelling reason to assume anything other than the developers going, &quot;So what? If someone goes through all the effort of getting a mundane sword into the Umbra, let them stab a bane with it. It's not going to break the game, and there's plenty of myths of heroes armed with normal weapons entering spirit worlds and getting into fights with spirits that don't end with, 'you don't have a magic sword, you can't do jack shit, you die now.;&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That is, if the spirit has such things. If the spirit is just a string of silvery light swirling around, then well .... just hit it with something. </div> </div> </div>There's a fairly massive excluded middle here of: spirits have the shapes and functions of what they represent, but it's all made of ephemera and as long as they have sufficient Essence it keeps functioning as normal. When a spirit runs out of Essene, it disembodies. It turns into that swirling light as it fades to escape. That's why every spirit gets the Re-form Charm for free.. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Garou mysticism is supposed to be intuitive in contrast to hermetic magic with it's strict rules. </div> </div> </div>Garou mysticism is also supposed to be highly ritualistic. It's not like there's a meaningful cost to using Talisman Dedication a lot; whether you want to swap your dedicated gear around, or the ST rules that giving it to a kin for a tune up undedicates it. We're talking about something that takes a few minutes to do as it's total cost once learned.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-13T05:20:21-07:00","id":1480953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1480609-combatting-spirits-with-normal-weapons?p=1480948#post1480948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's being removed from the game by mundane weapons brought into the Umbra working in spirit-combat when that's always been the rules? Even if it wasn't intentional in 1e, they never changed it. Even the CofD didn't fully change this despite changing other things around this that shows that the developers were aware of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>We misunderstood each other. I wasn't referencing to the weapon, but to seeing spirits as having no internal organs, being just essence, epherma and all that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1480609-combatting-spirits-with-normal-weapons?p=1480948#post1480948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a fairly massive excluded middle here of: spirits have the shapes and functions of what they represent, but it's all made of ephemera and as long as they have sufficient Essence it keeps functioning as normal.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, within the scope of spirit combat rules.<br /> Also, all spirits can fly, for some reason, so actually ripping the legs off of a spider spirit wouldn't hinder its movement one bit and with no wound penalties such an action makes no sense mechanically.<br /> <br /> That's what I mean with that it takes away from the game narratively. The most grotesque monsters a Garou might face are spirits/banes. So, a dangerous yet heroic feat like jumping into a open jaws of a terrasque-like bane and then ripping one's way from the throat to the heart makes for an interesting action sequence, but is senseless in regards to the game mechanics.<br /> <br /> So, my point is, that for most of the spirits in the middle, who have shapes recognisable as eyes, heads, jaws, legs, bellys, claws and so on, players should be able to come up with alternative strategies and not be hindered by the inadequate generalisation that are the spirit combat rules.<br /> <br /> Meaning, arrows aimed for the eyes of the monster should blind it, not be met with &quot;it just has the shape of an eye, but is actually epherma and the bane doesn't get penalties from being wounded&quot;. One could handle it that way, sure, but I'd recommend against it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1480609-combatting-spirits-with-normal-weapons?p=1480948#post1480948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> When a spirit runs out of Essene, it disembodies. It turns into that swirling light as it fades to escape. That's why every spirit gets the Re-form Charm for free..</div> </div> </div> </div>Does it?<br /> I think it falls into Slumber right there. To Re-Form is an action, requiring a Gnosis roll (as of revised, not sure about W20). Garou can kill spirits that lost all their essence and harvest Gnosis for themselves in the process.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1480609-combatting-spirits-with-normal-weapons?p=1480948#post1480948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Garou mysticism is also supposed to be highly ritualistic. It's not like there's a meaningful cost to using Talisman Dedication a lot; whether you want to swap your dedicated gear around, or the ST rules that giving it to a kin for a tune up undedicates it. We're talking about something that takes a few minutes to do as it's total cost once learned.</div> </div> </div> </div>If an ST rules handing the sword to another person for maintenance would un-dedicate it, so be it. I wouldn't.<br /> Still, there is the issue of possible failure or botch on the roll and the question at which point swapping out items in too rapid a succession becomes practice inherently dis-respecting the Rite or the spirits involved. This is when Renown and Gifts like &quot;<i>Sense Chiminage&quot;</i> become involved.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-13T13:02:44-07:00","id":1480992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1480609-combatting-spirits-with-normal-weapons?p=1480953#post1480953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We misunderstood each other. I wasn't referencing to the weapon, but to seeing spirits as having no internal organs, being just essence, epherma and all that.</div> </div> </div> </div>But what's been &quot;removed&quot; in that case? It's not like every combat maneuver is meant to be applicable to every situation. There are explicitly fomori without eyes, so you can't eye gouge them. That doesn't &quot;remove&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> True, within the scope of spirit combat rules.<br /> Also, all spirits can fly, for some reason, so actually ripping the legs off of a spider spirit wouldn't hinder its movement one bit and with no wound penalties such an action makes no sense mechanically. </div> </div> </div>Hrm. It's almost like fighting spirits effectively is a highly specialized skill set that requires training above and beyond normal mundane tactics... like some of the Pack Tactics that let you mess up spirits.<br /> <br /> The whole point I'm trying to make, and feels entirely supported by the rules and text in general, is that you can attack a spirit with a normal sword and hurt it. It's just far from optimal in the vast majority of cases. Replacing &quot;sword&quot; with &quot;combat maneuver,&quot; doesn't really change anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...makes for an interesting action sequence, but is senseless in regards to the game mechanics. </div> </div> </div>Which is true about WoD combat in general. It's not a combat system for replicating big awesome combat set pieces from action movies.<br /> <br /> Even if spirits worked like physical creatures, this would still be true. There's a reason Exalted and Storypath have to change so much to make these sorts of things actually functional.<br /> <br /> And really... I'd say this is entirely intentional for WtA: the Garou want to be epic action badasses in a war where that's suicidal. They're driven to be legends in a battle where that generally just means you die a horrible ugly death for not fighting smart instead. Legends are the tiny fraction of Garou that survived doing crazy stunts in the past and everyone forgot the dead that didn't. The living movers and shakers of the Garou Nation are in charge because they're generally pragmatic minded people and thus actually effective leaders that have minimal competition for their jobs because of all the Garou that keep dying trying to be awesome.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, my point is, that for most of the spirits in the middle, who have shapes recognisable as eyes, heads, jaws, legs, bellys, claws and so on, players should be able to come up with alternative strategies and not be hindered by the inadequate generalisation that are the spirit combat rules. </div> </div> </div>Perhaps though, these should be supernaturally based to deal with supernatural problems? Like Pack Tactics (which require a Totem/etc. to bond the pack, and Gnosis within the pack); which finally have some rules for making your own.<br /> <br /> The combat system really doesn't work well for what you're talking about if you let mundane combat tactics override things that make supernaturals dangerous. A spirit with 50 Essence shouldn't be rendered harmless because you got a successful called shot in. Spirits are mostly dangerous because they have gigantic piles of &quot;health&quot; compared to other things (even if they also need that to power Charms). That's the abstraction that makes fighting them particularly difficult. Beating them without having to deal with their big pools of Essence isn't encouraging &quot;creative&quot; combat tactics. It's just creating a new optimal combat approach.<br /> <br /> Imagine if staking a vampire only required 1 success and ignored damage/soak. All of VtM combat would revolve around staking, because you can ignore 12+ soak and 7+ HL by taking a small difficulty increase. Changing spirit combat needs to avoid that outcome.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does it? </div> </div> </div>Yes? You basically rephrased exactly what I was saying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Still, there is the issue of possible failure or botch on the roll and the question at which point swapping out items in too rapid a succession becomes practice inherently dis-respecting the Rite or the spirits involved. This is when Renown and Gifts like &quot;<i>Sense Chiminage&quot;</i> become involved.<br /> </div> </div> </div>OK, really, what's the point? Are you just going to keep stretching and stretching and stretching?<br /> <br /> 1) Why would you roll 99.9% of these rites? That's against the spirit of the rules. Of the remainder, why wouldn't you allow the automatic success rules to apply since Talisman Dedication doesn't scale with successes rolled?<br /> <br /> 2) What book ever indicates that you'd be disrespecting spirits by using Talisman Dedication a lot?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-13T13:41:05-07:00","id":1481001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You're not using logic, you're trying to dress up your opinions and preferences as logic </div> </div> </div>No, I'm using common sense, but if you think one can kill an ondine using a jar of mayonnaise, that's fine lol. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but if a spirit manifests in the physical world a kin can still shot it, and damage it. </div> </div> </div>Naturally, but then the spirit is MATERIALIZED in the physical world, then it can naturally be damaged by anything that would damage a MATERIAL being in our world.<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter who's swinging the fucking sword, if it's mundane, i.e. not made of ephemera or anything compatible with spirits it WILL NOT hurt the spirit's pattern, and it shouldn't even stay long in the umbra as it naturally doesn't belong there.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-13T16:03:46-07:00","id":1481020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1480609-combatting-spirits-with-normal-weapons?p=1481001#post1481001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I'm using common sense..</div> </div> </div> </div>What happened to logic?<br /> <br /> And you're not using common sense, because common sense would be the supernatural creatures in a RPG have whatever powers/abilities/etc. that the RPG says they have, not what some random fan rants about on the Internet. You're using troll-rant arguments.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...but if you think one can kill an ondine using a jar of mayonnaise, that's fine lol. </div> </div> </div><br /> Mayo has Banality10 and is well known for killing Selkie and Merfolk changelings just by being in the same room at them. Throwing mayo at them is the worst crime a fae soul is capable of.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Naturally, but then the spirit is MATERIALIZED in the physical world, then it can naturally be damaged by anything that would damage a MATERIAL being in our world. </div> </div> </div>And... the same is true of the metaphysical process of bringing physical objects into the Umbra. Once you bring a sword into the Umbra, it exists in the Umbra in a fashion that lets it interact naturally with Umbral entities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It doesn't matter who's swinging the fucking sword, if it's mundane, i.e. not made of ephemera or anything compatible with spirits it WILL NOT hurt the spirit's pattern, and it shouldn't even stay long in the umbra as it naturally doesn't belong there. </div> </div> </div>That's not how the Umbra works in the WoD. The longer material plane objects stay in the Umbra, they become more ephemeral rather than getting spat out into the physical plane. If you leave a mundane sword in the Umbra long enough, it will become an object of mundane ephemera instead of mundane metal.<br /> <br /> I get there is a lot of &quot;how I want things to be&quot; in your posts, but if you keep claiming your preferences and opinions are &quot;facts,&quot; &quot;logic,&quot; or &quot;common sense,&quot; I'm going to keep calling it out for the bullshit it is. Especially in a thread where someone was trying to get an answer about how the game works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-13T17:11:03-07:00","id":1481027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1480609-combatting-spirits-with-normal-weapons?p=1481020#post1481020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mayo has Banality10 and is well known for killing Selkie and Merfolk changelings just by being in the same room at them. Throwing mayo at them is the worst crime a fae soul is capable of.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=puZT1Aii8aw\" target=\"_blank\">Behold - the face of the Autumn People!</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-13T17:34:55-07:00","id":1481029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm going to keep calling it out for the bullshit it is </div> </div> </div>Oh, little poor thing... You're the only one here saying bullshit and acting as if your oversimplified metaphysical interpretation of the WoD is gospel truth...<br /> <br /> Back to the topic, the form the spirit assumes is always going to be important, so one can't expect to harm a mist or a storm, or even a tangible shade (like the one a vampire with Obtenebration 5 can turn himself into) with a mundane knife/sword or a .38 revolver. One can understand this basic things, not only by using his brain or just by reading the description of powers and imagine, rightfully so, that a spirit could emulate these powers in any realm. In any case, most of the time, if you're in umbra, you can usually harm him, and he can harm you just as easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-13T19:57:59-07:00","id":1481036,"title":"","content":"Spirits do not naturally have multiple &quot;forms&quot; to assume (maybe you'd stop having your posts called bullshit if you actually posted stuff that's in the books).<br /> <br /> If a spirit has a Charm that allows them to change forms (like the Disciplines you keep referencing for some reason in a WtA thread) or become immaterial? Then they can use those Charms and gain the benefits of them. What the rules don't have is those as innate powers spirit. We know what the default all-spirits-get-them Charms are.<br /> <br /> How about you actually reference a WtA book instead of vaguely referencing random WoD books and saying, &quot;spirits should be able to copy these powers completely with no consideration for how spirits work.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-14T04:37:43-07:00","id":1481058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1480609-combatting-spirits-with-normal-weapons?p=1480992#post1480992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But what's been &quot;removed&quot; in that case? It's not like every combat maneuver is meant to be applicable to every situation. There are explicitly fomori without eyes, so you can't eye gouge them. That doesn't &quot;remove&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a qualitative difference between one type of fomori and applying similar rules to all spirits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1480609-combatting-spirits-with-normal-weapons?p=1480992#post1480992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole point I'm trying to make, and feels entirely supported by the rules and text in general, is that you can attack a spirit with a normal sword and hurt it. It's just far from optimal in the vast majority of cases.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. Like I said, that wasn't the point I wanted to dispute.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1480609-combatting-spirits-with-normal-weapons?p=1480992#post1480992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And really... I'd say this is entirely intentional for WtA: the Garou want to be epic action badasses in a war where that's suicidal. They're driven to be legends in a battle where that generally just means you die a horrible ugly death for not fighting smart instead. Legends are the tiny fraction of Garou that survived doing crazy stunts in the past and everyone forgot the dead that didn't. The living movers and shakers of the Garou Nation are in charge because they're generally pragmatic minded people and thus actually effective leaders that have minimal competition for their jobs because of all the Garou that keep dying trying to be awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but wouldn't that call for a combat system more like Exalted? I mean, the PCs aren't necessarily meant to be these Legends, so the system should give them an incentive to die horrible ugly deaths and have fun with it...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1480609-combatting-spirits-with-normal-weapons?p=1480992#post1480992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps though, these should be supernaturally based to deal with supernatural problems? Like Pack Tactics (which require a Totem/etc. to bond the pack, and Gnosis within the pack); which finally have some rules for making your own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on what level of supernatural we are talking about. Is grabbing ephermal dirt from the penumbral ground and throw it into the bane's tiny eyes supernatural enough dirty fighting, or does it require mundane dirt dedicated via Rite or carried in the umbra by fetish or is all that to low on supernatural?<br /> I generally would feel that having sidestepped is supernatural enough for most spirit interaction. But sure, tastes can differ here... <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1480609-combatting-spirits-with-normal-weapons?p=1480992#post1480992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The combat system really doesn't work well for what you're talking about if you let mundane combat tactics override things that make supernaturals dangerous. A spirit with 50 Essence shouldn't be rendered harmless because you got a successful called shot in. Spirits are mostly dangerous because they have gigantic piles of &quot;health&quot; compared to other things (even if they also need that to power Charms). That's the abstraction that makes fighting them particularly difficult. Beating them without having to deal with their big pools of Essence isn't encouraging &quot;creative&quot; combat tactics. It's just creating a new optimal combat approach.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, there is a need for balancing and serving a narrative need. I wouldn't also think that one called shot the the eyes would render a powerful bane &quot;harmless&quot;. There bane might just change attack tactics from claws to tackle and full body slam, or something like that. There should be a reward for creativity that is suitable for the situation.<br /> <br /> Imagine if staking a vampire only required 1 success and ignored damage/soak. All of VtM combat would revolve around staking, because you can ignore 12+ soak and 7+ HL by taking a small difficulty increase. Changing spirit combat needs to avoid that outcome.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1480609-combatting-spirits-with-normal-weapons?p=1480992#post1480992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes? You basically rephrased exactly what I was saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me &quot;When a spirit runs out of Essene, it disembodies. It turns into that swirling light as it fades to escape.&quot; read as if it was a given that any spirit that hit Essence 0 would automatically disembody and fade to escape. That is, imo, not the case.<br /> A spirit that is low on Essence would, imo, take an action to re-form (since it requires a roll). If that opportunity is missed, and the spirit is reduced to 0 Essence, the spirit is doomed to fall into Slumber right there - but doesn't disembody. It can be slain and parts of its body can be harvested (like a fang to create a Fang Dagger).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1480609-combatting-spirits-with-normal-weapons?p=1480992#post1480992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, really, what's the point? Are you just going to keep stretching and stretching and stretching?<br /> <br /> 1) Why would you roll 99.9% of these rites? That's against the spirit of the rules. Of the remainder, why wouldn't you allow the automatic success rules to apply since Talisman Dedication doesn't scale with successes rolled?<br /> <br /> 2) What book ever indicates that you'd be disrespecting spirits by using Talisman Dedication a lot?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the general section on Rites states they should be rolled. And, yeah, maybe it is stretching. W20 now states that Rites are expected to work, like a stone is expected to fall down. So, it seems the Pact is somehow responsible for the Rites to work, but it isn't so much the collective of spirits powering them, but a law of nature, it seems. Therefore one could argue, that it is totally okay to do the Rite every 15 Minutes or so. Since Mytsic Rites are usually performed alone, one isn't wasting the time of other garou, either.<br /> <br /> It still doesn't fit with my taste for Rites and how they should be regarded by the Garou (or Fera). We don't know how the specific Auspice versions of the Rite look like, but if they have any part where the garou asks the spirits assistance it is hard to regard this as sincere after the 20th time a day.<br /> W20 also did tone down that it was inappropriate to use the Rite outside of one's own moon phase.<br /> <br /> In the end, I can hardly think of a reason to perform the Rite that often, that is not either exploiting or otherwise showing bad judgement.<br /> &quot;I changed my mind, no I want to dedicate my Star Trek uniform again, for we might head to the Television Sub Domain.&quot; Done.<br /> &quot;No, wait, I need my Explorers Outfit and travel gear dedicated, so I have it for the travel...&quot;<br /> &quot;Make up your mind already&quot;.<br /> <br /> My believe could also be rooted in the word &quot;dedication&quot; and it's translation to German. In a narrative sense the item(s) become part of the garou, metaphysically, and in some forms even physically. To undedicate them and dedicate other items doesn't seem very dedicated in the first place. Faithful, loyal or devoted are all words that would by synonymous if dedicated is translated to German and back to English...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-14T14:09:14-07:00","id":1481119,"title":"","content":"..... Wow. So, this escalated. <br /> <br /> Thank you all for your feedback, I really do appreciate it, and it gives me a lot to chew over. (Also please be nice to each other, it's just a game and we're all nerds here.)<br /> <br /> &lt;3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23998-dynamiterave","name":"DynamiteRave","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-14T14:17:24-07:00","id":1481121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1480609-combatting-spirits-with-normal-weapons?p=1481058#post1481058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a qualitative difference between one type of fomori and applying similar rules to all spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>The rules for spirits are highly abstract. A good number of standard combat maneuvers don't even have a clear way of applying to them because they don't use normal traits for their actions, etc. What does throwing sand in a spirit's eyes do? You can't penalize Perception or Alertness, they don't have that. Penalizing all Gnosis rolls would be insanely overpowered for a simple dirty fighting trick. Using the Blinded complication is kinda meaningless when spirits don't need sensory organs to sense things; every spirit has Realm Sense which lets them spiritually sense everything around them as long as that Charm applies (something the Blinded complication indicates is supposed to negate its penalties).<br /> <br /> This is my contention with the word &quot;remove.&quot; You're saying that something was there, but now it isn't. But it was never there in the first place. We've never has a WtA which detailed spirit combat that puts spirits more in-line with standard combatants and lets you apply more complex tactics. More complicated spirit fights is always something that's needed to be added to the rule (officially when the writers want to make a statted out spirit more interesting to fight, or unofficially by STs).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> True, but wouldn't that call for a combat system more like Exalted? </div> </div> </div>Maybe? But that's a bit beyond the scope of this thread don't you think?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Depends on what level of supernatural we are talking about. </div> </div> </div>I gave the example of pack tactics already.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I wouldn't also think that one called shot the the eyes would render a powerful bane &quot;harmless&quot; </div> </div> </div>The problem is they only have three stats to penalize. If you slap a -2 penalty on Willpower and Gnosis rolls on them... it's a huge decrease in their potential to be a threat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Therefore one could argue, that it is totally okay to do the Rite every 15 Minutes or so. Since Mytsic Rites are usually performed alone, one isn't wasting the time of other garou, either. </div> </div> </div>And yet, nobody is actually arguing that. Just that there's no inherent penalty for using the Rite a lot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My believe could also be rooted in the word &quot;dedication&quot; and it's translation to German. In a narrative sense the item(s) become part of the garou, metaphysically, and in some forms even physically. To undedicate them and dedicate other items doesn't seem very dedicated in the first place. Faithful, loyal or devoted are all words that would by synonymous if dedicated is translated to German and back to English... </div> </div> </div>Dedicate, in English, can also mean something closer to &quot;assign,&quot; though it does carry the connotations of a longer than usual assignment of a resource to a project/etc.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-14T14:51:10-07:00","id":1481129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Orig